From: Omer Dangoor <omerdn1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:09:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ios): stop the session's xcodebuild when its runner has
 died

LocalXCTestInstaller.uninstall() returned early when the runner no longer
answered, before it stopped the xcodebuild test-without-building process it
had started. When a runner dies, that xcodebuild keeps running, so a dead MCP
session that #3385 rebuilds left one xcodebuild behind per rebuild, alongside
the new session's xcodebuild on the same simulator.

uninstall() now stops the xcodebuild it started before it checks the runner,
waiting up to 10 seconds for it to exit before killing it.

start() stops that xcodebuild too when the runner doesn't answer within the
startup timeout. Nothing else did: maestro test registers its cleanup only
after the driver has opened, so a runner that never came up left its
xcodebuild running after Maestro exited.

The installer takes XCRunnerCLIUtils and the startup timeout as constructor
parameters, so the tests can launch a stand-in xcodebuild and time out
quickly. The timeout still defaults to MAESTRO_DRIVER_STARTUP_TIMEOUT.
